# Composite (ADR-009): a file that has BOTH an all-capture lambda (KEUR-CPP-001)
# AND a stored/returned lambda (KEUR-CPP-002) is the real dangling-reference
# shape — a [&]/[=] lambda kept past its scope. Either leaf alone is weak
# (a direct-call [&] is safe; storing a no-capture lambda is fine); together
# they are the pattern Sonar's data-flow flags. The engine stays dumb — the
# "both matter" logic is DATA here, like KEUR-IAC-010.
# @see docs/adr/ADR-040-engine-coverage-gaps.md
# @implements ADR-009.composite ADR-040
id: KEUR-CPP-003
ilities: [analysability]
maturity: 5
title: Stored all-capture lambda — likely dangling reference
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: composite
action: warn
confidence: 0.65
composite:
  all: KEUR-CPP-001 KEUR-CPP-002
message: "This file both captures a whole scope in a lambda ([&]/[=]) AND stores/returns a lambda — the dangling-reference shape. Give the stored lambda an explicit capture list and capture by value (or a shared owner) if it outlives the scope. @see KEUR-CPP-003"
fix: "Replace [&]/[=] with an explicit capture list; for a lambda stored in a member or returned, capture by value rather than by reference."
